  "limitations": [
    "Remediation of the attempt-01 and attempt-02 findings is documented in docs/planning/reviews/C01/remediation-attempt-01.md and remediation-attempt-02.md; the latter also lists three defects found during native acceptance after remediation (one driver defect, two app focus/zoom defects) and their fixes. Superseded native runs are retained with causes under docs/planning/evidence/C01/native-failed/.",
    "Native visual evidence is fixture-only WKWebView self-capture (Fixture > Capture Window), not a screen recording. The snapshot spans the WKWebView's 820pt bounds while web content occupies the 788pt below the title bar (AX: AXWebArea at [95,69] size [1280,788]; the rail fills it to the window bottom), so every capture shows a ~32pt strip at the bottom that is outside the visible viewport. In captures/standard/zoom-200.png the Academy rail fill is pointer hover: the AX snapshot for that step shows aria-current=page only on Settings and Academy not focused.",
    "Spoken VoiceOver output was not recorded; accessibility is evidenced through the AX tree (roles, names, aria-current, focus) driven by System Events. Startup network evidence is 0.5s socket sampling over 15s (DNS via mDNSResponder not attributable).",
    "The clean-checkout reproduction (evidence/C01/clean-checkout/summary.json) passed check and test from a fresh Academy clone at 891f65ee; its run records show a different source fingerprint only because the fresh git init lacked the origin remote in .git/config (part of the source fingerprint); with identical .git/config the clean tree's own xtask reports the reviewed fingerprints.",
    "No signing, notarization, live API, installed-package or SDK work is in C01 scope; those are C02+ and C25-C26."
  ],
